I felt a gut-wrenching sense of dread before diving into this game. Modern gaming has taught me to keep my expectations low, making me cynical about anything I might actually enjoy.\n\nBoy, was I wrong.\n\nThis game is everything a Space Marine fan could hope for. Even if you’re an outsider or not particularly into 40K, you’ll still find plenty to enjoy.\n\nWhile it’s not a game that will rake in 10/10 scores, it excels at what it set out to do. Its sole intention? Pure, unadulterated fun.\n\nI played this with a friend who had zero exposure to 40K lore, and both of us were hyped from the very first cutscene. From there, it only got better. The adrenaline rush from the combat and the epic set pieces was fantastic. Combat felt gruesome, heavy, and exhilarating. As a Space Marine, you’re a genetically modified transhuman killing machine, and the gameplay hammers that point home by rewarding aggressive play. Survival isn’t about hiding or running—it's about charging into the fray, fighting, and killing. The combat gives you that primal, masculine urge to keep the mayhem going.\n\nThe attention to detail from the developers was genuinely refreshing. It’s clear they approached this license with a lot of respect and didn’t try to bastardize it for monetary gain.\n\nAnd that’s exactly why this game deserves every bit of its success. It feels like it was made with the player in mind—a piece of art crafted for enjoyment, not a soulless product designed to milk us of our hard-earned cash.\n\nThe game isn’t without its flaws, though. The campaign is short (I finished it in about 8–10 hours), and the gameplay loop can feel repetitive. That said, its brevity worked in its favor. The game didn’t overstay its welcome; if anything, I found myself wanting more.\n\nIn an industry obsessed with complex, interwoven narratives and overly ambitious characters, Space Marine 2 embraces simplicity. Its story exists to tie the action together and make sense of the chaos, but it’s straightforward enough to let you focus on the gameplay.\n\nThis game isn’t trying to be the second coming of Jesus or the best game ever made. Its goal is simply to entertain, and it nails that.\n\nAs a 40K fan and someone fed up with mediocrity in modern gaming, I’m tempted to give it a 10/10. Realistically, though, an 8.5/10 feels more accurate.\n\nIf you’ve been searching for something to satisfy your inner child, I highly recommend it.", "timestamp_created": 1734302489, "timestamp_updated": 1734302489, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 0, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": 0.5, "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1725898212", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "182853662", "author": {"steamid": "76561199763421289", "personaname": "Cammobammo", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/profiles/76561199763421289/", "num_games_owned": 0, "num_reviews": 1, "playtime_forever": 276, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 276, "last_played": 1734302311, "avatar": "e0d4d881c5ecf7dfe45c7907506c17b23485ec62"}, "language": "english", "review": "yes", "timestamp_created": 1734302328, "timestamp_updated": 1734302328, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 0, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": 0.5, "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": false, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1725898212", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "182853318", "author": {"steamid": "76561198047490685", "personaname": "Silver", "persona_status": "online", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/profiles/76561198047490685/", "num_games_owned": 0, "num_reviews": 19, "playtime_forever": 10757, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 6636, "last_played": 1776615630, "avatar": "531d9102586af8b2a263c46f81b13475d55805e9"}, "language": "english", "review": "I have always wanted a 40k game that was cool enough to introduce to my friends who don't know what 40k is and is cool enough to have mainstream appeal. This game can show to anyone why I love the lore so much and why I find 40k so cool. It is the piece of pop culture media I have been waiting for my life.\r\n\r\n11/10 would recommend any time any situation", "timestamp_created": 1734301966, "timestamp_updated": 1734301966, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 0, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": 0.5, "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1725898212", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "182853251", "author": {"steamid": "76561199224760216", "personaname": "MilliMx2", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/profiles/76561199224760216/", "num_games_owned": 0, "num_reviews": 9, "playtime_forever": 1672, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 1282, "last_played": 1745795744, "avatar": "860045ea130d2f6ff9214e64f22f657de7899079"}, "language": "english", "review": "A refreshing reminder of what the gaming industry has strayed from", "timestamp_created": 1734301889, "timestamp_updated": 1734301889, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 0, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": 0.5, "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1725898212", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "182852570", "author": {"steamid": "76561198038094329", "personaname": "DropDeads", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/id/Dr0pDeads/", "num_games_owned": 0, "num_reviews": 2, "playtime_forever": 2122, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 1806, "last_played": 1745059648, "avatar": "02215f